  m_Name: Object_44
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Engine Mount
  description: The Engine Mount is a large, elongated component located at the middle-center-center
    of the engine, made of metal-mid material. Its primary function is to secure
    the engine to the aircraft frame, absorbing vibrations and stresses while maintaining
    engine alignment. Notably, the engine mount's design and material help to minimize
    vibration transmission to the airframe, reducing noise and improving overall
    aircraft comfort and safety.
